          %h3#remark Remark
          %p
            The third axiom implies that the existential quantification occurring in the fourth axioms is unique thus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕂
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
            is indeed
            = succeed "." do
              %em cartesian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+algebraic+theory"} essentially algebraic
            in the syntactic sense, though, of course, it is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+equivalence"} Morita equivalent
            to an essentially algebraic axiomatisation. Other signatures, like a single sorted “arrows only” one, are also possible, the one used here (taken from Johnstone
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#J77"} 1977
            %strong elementary theory of abstract categories
            as presented in Lawvere (
            %a{:href => "#Law66"}> 1966
            ).
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p Foremost, we have
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi 𝕂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi cat
